      "claim": "No legally recognized organization called the Confederate States Army exists today; groups that use Confederate symbols are private reenactment clubs or militias, not an official army.",
      "evidence": "U.S. law (e.g., Title 10 of the United States Code) defines the armed forces as the Army, Navy, Air Force, Marine Corps, Coast Guard, and National Guard; there is no provision for a Confederate military entity.",
